# Single stage docker files can be used for dev,test environments. But for production, we use multi stage.

# We can use one stage for the dependencies (build stage) and the application runtime in another stage in a multi stage dockerfile

The key idea: two separate, independent containers

Think of each FROM as starting a brand new, empty computer. The two stages don’t share anything unless you explicitly copy files between them.

Build phase needs heavy tools (compilers, package managers, dev dependencies). Run phase needs almost nothing. Multi-stage means: do phase 1 in a fat image, copy only the output into a thin image for phase 2.

< Multi stage dockerfile for a Node app >

FROM node:22-alpine as dependencies
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci

FROM node:22-alpine as build
WORKDIR /app
COPY --from=dependencies /app/nod_modules ./node_modules
COPY . .
RUN npm run build

FROM node:22-alpine as prod
WORKDIR /app
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm ci --omit=dev
COPY --from=build ./app/dist ./dist
EXPOSE 3000
USER node
CMD ["node", "dist/server.js"]










